tasks.prompt:
A triangle $\triangle ABC$ is given, for which $A(1;1)$, $B(6;-3)$ and $C(10;-2)$. If $AM$ $(M \in BC)$ and $AD$ $(D \in BC)$ are respectively the median and the altitude of $\triangle ABC$, find:

a) the general equation of the line $AM$;

b) the Cartesian equation of the line $AD$;

c) the cosine of the angle between the median $AM$ and the altitude $AD$ of $\triangle ABC$.
